1
00:00:00,480 --> 00:00:01,740
Hello, everyone.

2
00:00:01,770 --> 00:00:03,000
This is Lilly.

3
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:08,010
And today we are going to talk about reported speech.

4
00:00:09,470 --> 00:00:10,100
Okay.

5
00:00:10,100 --> 00:00:13,070
So what is reported speech?

6
00:00:13,130 --> 00:00:18,740
We use reported speech to say what another person said.

7
00:00:21,160 --> 00:00:22,210
For example.

8
00:00:23,050 --> 00:00:27,980
Bill Gates said: your most unhappy customers are your greatest source

9
00:00:28,120 --> 00:00:30,370
greatest source of learning.

10
00:00:31,560 --> 00:00:37,530
Now we read this quote, you liked it and you want to tell someone about it.

11
00:00:37,800 --> 00:00:43,200
You want to tell someone what Bill Gates said. You would say:

12
00:00:43,620 --> 00:00:50,310
Bill Gates said that your most unhappy customers were your greatest source of learning.

13
00:00:52,250 --> 00:00:57,620
Did you notice what changed here compared to the original quote?

14
00:01:01,200 --> 00:01:01,830
Yeah.

15
00:01:02,250 --> 00:01:05,400
Are changed to were. 

16
00:01:06,510 --> 00:01:16,050
So that's what happens when we report someone's speech, report what someone said. Tenses shift.

17
00:01:18,320 --> 00:01:18,990
All right.

18
00:01:19,580 --> 00:01:29,180
So the direct speech would be, for example, someone said, my Internet connection is really slow today.

19
00:01:29,960 --> 00:01:31,480
That's what someone said, right

20
00:01:31,490 --> 00:01:34,100
My Internet connection is really slow today.

21
00:01:35,360 --> 00:01:39,140
Then you are reporting what they said.

22
00:01:39,140 --> 00:01:41,630
So hear reported speech.

23
00:01:42,880 --> 00:01:47,560
Kaia said her Internet connection was really slow.

24
00:01:49,300 --> 00:01:52,240
So is changes to was. 

25
00:01:53,510 --> 00:01:56,840
Present simple changes to past simple.

26
00:01:58,170 --> 00:01:58,910
Okay.

27
00:01:58,920 --> 00:02:02,130
And of course, you would change my to her.

28
00:02:02,160 --> 00:02:03,510
That's logical, right

29
00:02:03,690 --> 00:02:05,820
She said my internet connection.

30
00:02:05,820 --> 00:02:12,090
And when you report this, you say Kaia said her Internet connection, right

31
00:02:14,750 --> 00:02:15,650
The next one.

32
00:02:15,650 --> 00:02:18,320
We are having a meeting-free day tomorrow.

33
00:02:19,690 --> 00:02:26,650
That's direct speech and the reported speech would be James said we were having a meeting-free day

34
00:02:26,650 --> 00:02:27,520
tomorrow.

35
00:02:28,560 --> 00:02:32,640
So are having - present continuous - changes to

36
00:02:33,620 --> 00:02:43,070
past continuous - were having. Generally all present tenses change to past tenses.

37
00:02:43,070 --> 00:02:43,840
Right

38
00:02:43,850 --> 00:02:45,140
So what do I mean?

39
00:02:45,680 --> 00:02:49,250
Present simple changes to past simple.

40
00:02:49,460 --> 00:02:54,890
Present continuous to past continuous, right and so on.

41
00:02:55,970 --> 00:03:00,260
The next one I will send you the job offer by 12 p.m.

42
00:03:01,310 --> 00:03:05,330
That's direct speech and the reported one would be The

43
00:03:05,360 --> 00:03:09,590
HR said she would send me the job offer by 12 p.m.

44
00:03:11,190 --> 00:03:13,800
So will changes to

45
00:03:14,570 --> 00:03:15,230
would.

46
00:03:15,770 --> 00:03:16,370
Right.

47
00:03:18,280 --> 00:03:19,030
Okay.

48
00:03:19,030 --> 00:03:23,770
The next one, we didn't get any complaints from users.

49
00:03:25,430 --> 00:03:30,140
Tom said they hadn't got any complaints from users.

50
00:03:31,640 --> 00:03:36,260
Past simple changes to past perfect.

51
00:03:37,470 --> 00:03:38,280
Mm hmm.

52
00:03:39,190 --> 00:03:41,230
That that one you have to remember,

53
00:03:41,230 --> 00:03:48,550
right, because as I said, all present time tenses change to past and past

54
00:03:48,550 --> 00:03:51,880
simple changes to past perfect.

55
00:03:53,490 --> 00:03:54,840
All right.

56
00:03:55,380 --> 00:03:57,090
And the next one.

57
00:03:57,540 --> 00:03:58,380
Oh, sorry.

58
00:03:58,680 --> 00:04:01,080
Let's also pay attention to we.

59
00:04:01,080 --> 00:04:03,270
We changed to they here,

60
00:04:03,270 --> 00:04:04,110
right.

61
00:04:05,480 --> 00:04:09,590
Because just imagine the situation.

62
00:04:10,100 --> 00:04:13,700
Someone said we didn't get any complaints from users.

63
00:04:13,730 --> 00:04:15,470
Now you're reporting this.

64
00:04:15,470 --> 00:04:16,220
So you say

65
00:04:16,250 --> 00:04:22,280
Tom said they hadn't got any complaints from users. Here

66
00:04:22,280 --> 00:04:23,570
we did not change.

67
00:04:23,600 --> 00:04:25,310
We are having a meeting-free day.

68
00:04:25,340 --> 00:04:30,800
James said we were having a meeting-free day because maybe it applies to all of us.

69
00:04:30,800 --> 00:04:34,940
So here you have to think, do I need to change a pronoun or not?

70
00:04:36,160 --> 00:04:36,810
Okay.

71
00:04:37,150 --> 00:04:43,270
And the last one, the company has increased its revenue by 20%.

72
00:04:44,970 --> 00:04:50,340
Our manager said that the company had increased its revenue by 20%.

73
00:04:52,840 --> 00:05:03,490
Okay so present perfect changes to past perfect too. Both tenses, past simple and present perfect, change

74
00:05:03,490 --> 00:05:05,620
to past perfect.

75
00:05:07,650 --> 00:05:08,460
This is it.

76
00:05:08,610 --> 00:05:13,740
This is the reported speech, but only sentences.

77
00:05:15,180 --> 00:05:18,270
The next one. Modals. 

78
00:05:18,480 --> 00:05:21,000
How do we report modals?

79
00:05:21,120 --> 00:05:22,910
There are some peculiarities here.

80
00:05:22,920 --> 00:05:24,000
We will look at them.

81
00:05:24,840 --> 00:05:31,230
Modals like words like may, must, right, should and so on.. can.

82
00:05:32,610 --> 00:05:37,620
So their direct speech is. Chao may have a solution to this problem.

83
00:05:39,160 --> 00:05:40,630
Then you report this.

84
00:05:41,020 --> 00:05:45,550
James said Chao might have a solution to that problem.

85
00:05:46,450 --> 00:05:50,370
So may changes to might.

86
00:05:50,410 --> 00:05:51,160
You're right.

87
00:05:51,760 --> 00:05:52,780
The next one.

88
00:05:53,050 --> 00:05:55,410
We must eliminate this bug

89
00:05:55,450 --> 00:05:56,260
asap.

90
00:05:57,210 --> 00:05:58,470
As soon as possible.

91
00:05:59,440 --> 00:06:03,880
Our team leader said we had to eliminate this bug asap.

92
00:06:06,050 --> 00:06:17,450
So must changes to had to. This is not so obvious as may and might, so please remember must changes to

93
00:06:17,480 --> 00:06:21,380
had to. And the last one can.

94
00:06:21,560 --> 00:06:23,600
I can't come to the party tomorrow.

95
00:06:23,600 --> 00:06:25,070
It's my son's birthday.

96
00:06:25,370 --> 00:06:29,570
He said he couldn't come to the party the next day.

97
00:06:29,870 --> 00:06:32,750
So can't changed to couldn't.

98
00:06:34,830 --> 00:06:43,380
Okay, can to could, may to might, must to had to and the rest of the modals stay the same.

99
00:06:43,380 --> 00:06:51,660
So for example, if you had should We should eliminate this bug then it would just stay.

100
00:06:51,690 --> 00:06:54,240
He said we should eliminate this bug.

101
00:06:55,870 --> 00:06:57,030
All right.

102
00:06:57,040 --> 00:06:59,440
This is it about reporting modals.

103
00:07:00,070 --> 00:07:03,070
And here are a few more little things.

104
00:07:04,160 --> 00:07:04,700
Look.

105
00:07:07,190 --> 00:07:12,260
Sometimes we would change in the reported speech tomorrow to the next day.

106
00:07:12,260 --> 00:07:14,870
Yesterday to the day before.

107
00:07:14,900 --> 00:07:16,580
Today to the same day.

108
00:07:16,730 --> 00:07:20,390
Like here, we're going to deal with it tomorrow.

109
00:07:20,990 --> 00:07:25,430
They said they were going to deal with it the next day.

110
00:07:26,930 --> 00:07:27,200
Here

111
00:07:27,200 --> 00:07:29,990
we change tomorrow to the next day.

112
00:07:31,840 --> 00:07:34,160
This will not always happen.

113
00:07:34,180 --> 00:07:37,630
I would say it's not always necessary to change it like this.

114
00:07:38,380 --> 00:07:40,450
You have to think about about it.

115
00:07:40,960 --> 00:07:43,540
You have to make sure it's easy to understand.

116
00:07:44,140 --> 00:07:47,040
And there will be like no misunderstanding.

117
00:07:47,050 --> 00:07:49,990
For example, someone said it on Monday.

118
00:07:49,990 --> 00:07:50,500
Right.

119
00:07:50,500 --> 00:07:52,690
We are going to deal with it tomorrow.

120
00:07:53,110 --> 00:07:54,700
You are saying this

121
00:07:54,700 --> 00:07:57,220
you are reporting this still on Monday.

122
00:07:57,340 --> 00:08:02,070
So you say they said they were going to deal with it tomorrow.

123
00:08:02,080 --> 00:08:04,930
You can keep tomorrow because

124
00:08:06,500 --> 00:08:09,130
tomorrow is still tomorrow for you.

125
00:08:09,140 --> 00:08:12,680
So it's still going to happen on Tuesday, right

126
00:08:13,550 --> 00:08:16,170
Like when when the person said it

127
00:08:16,190 --> 00:08:18,470
the original thing

128
00:08:18,470 --> 00:08:19,100
right

129
00:08:20,020 --> 00:08:21,880
By tomorrow we meant Tuesday.

130
00:08:21,880 --> 00:08:26,560
And now when we are reporting, we still mean Tuesday, then keep it.

131
00:08:27,160 --> 00:08:34,929
But when you are reporting this, when you are saying what this person said, like on Wednesday, right

132
00:08:35,169 --> 00:08:38,260
When they said tomorrow, they meant Tuesday.

133
00:08:38,260 --> 00:08:39,090
Right.

134
00:08:39,100 --> 00:08:41,080
But it's already Wednesday,

135
00:08:41,080 --> 00:08:49,510
when you are saying this, then it may change to change it to the next day to avoid misunderstanding.

136
00:08:49,960 --> 00:08:58,780
So that's how what I would do here, which logic I would follow here. With all of them

137
00:08:59,020 --> 00:09:02,200
with yesterday, with the same day and so on.

138
00:09:04,060 --> 00:09:07,300
Here may change to there.

139
00:09:07,390 --> 00:09:08,200
Like this.

140
00:09:08,200 --> 00:09:10,540
We meet here every Monday at nine.

141
00:09:10,570 --> 00:09:13,570
They said they met there every Monday at nine.

142
00:09:15,310 --> 00:09:15,940
Okay.

143
00:09:15,940 --> 00:09:17,020
And one more.

144
00:09:17,290 --> 00:09:19,420
I will fix this bug today.

145
00:09:19,450 --> 00:09:22,840
He said he would fix that bug the same day.

146
00:09:23,260 --> 00:09:27,520
So here changes to there, this changes to that.

147
00:09:27,520 --> 00:09:28,750
But again.

148
00:09:29,820 --> 00:09:33,910
If that helps understanding what the person said.

149
00:09:33,930 --> 00:09:34,590
Right.

150
00:09:34,770 --> 00:09:38,510
If that doesn't actually cause some confusion.

151
00:09:38,520 --> 00:09:40,100
So think think about it.

152
00:09:40,110 --> 00:09:43,350
Only you can decide if you change it or not.

153
00:09:45,060 --> 00:09:46,440
All right.

154
00:09:46,500 --> 00:09:48,030
And we move on.

155
00:09:48,960 --> 00:09:52,800
A little thing, say versus tell.

156
00:09:55,120 --> 00:09:58,510
When to use which. Look is easy.

157
00:09:58,630 --> 00:10:00,250
Just remember this.

158
00:10:00,680 --> 00:10:02,980
Tony said he was busy.

159
00:10:04,000 --> 00:10:07,640
We use, say without object or pronoun

160
00:10:07,660 --> 00:10:09,580
so what does it mean?

161
00:10:09,610 --> 00:10:10,750
It means we cannot say

162
00:10:10,750 --> 00:10:12,060
he said her,

163
00:10:12,070 --> 00:10:17,770
he said Jane, just Tony said he was busy.

164
00:10:17,770 --> 00:10:19,600
You don't say whom

165
00:10:19,600 --> 00:10:20,500
he said it.

166
00:10:21,440 --> 00:10:27,080
And if you want to say whom he said it, just say to tell, use tell.

167
00:10:27,110 --> 00:10:27,770
Right

168
00:10:28,160 --> 00:10:31,190
Tony told Camila he was busy.

169
00:10:31,460 --> 00:10:35,480
So you must use told with an object or pronoun.

170
00:10:36,200 --> 00:10:37,420
This means you can't say

171
00:10:37,430 --> 00:10:38,900
He told he was busy.

172
00:10:39,440 --> 00:10:40,970
He said he was busy.

173
00:10:41,300 --> 00:10:44,000
He told Camila he was busy.

174
00:10:45,910 --> 00:10:46,540
All right.

175
00:10:46,540 --> 00:10:48,310
And now a little disclaimer.

176
00:10:49,280 --> 00:10:50,480
You can say

177
00:10:50,510 --> 00:10:54,710
Tony said to Camila he was busy.

178
00:10:54,710 --> 00:11:05,750
So you can use say with the person you are saying it to, but use to, okay. If you are not using to,

179
00:11:05,990 --> 00:11:08,890
then don't don't say it.

180
00:11:08,900 --> 00:11:11,270
Don't put the name up to say, right.

181
00:11:13,070 --> 00:11:21,380
So I would just follow actually the rule that I use say alone and I use tell with with the name after

182
00:11:21,380 --> 00:11:21,770
it.

183
00:11:23,660 --> 00:11:31,580
But I just don't want you to think, oh the teacher said we cannot say who we are saying this after say

184
00:11:31,580 --> 00:11:38,240
and now I see the sentence - Tony said to me - that's just because you inserted that "to" there.

185
00:11:39,800 --> 00:11:40,520
All right.

